{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/800807-experiences-playing-a-multi-sourcbook-game","id":800807,"title":"Experiences playing a multi sourcbook game.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-04T16:45:52-08:00","id":800807,"title":"Experiences playing a multi sourcbook game.","content":"What are your experiences playing a game with multiple types of creature? Like having a vampire, mage, and 2 changelings in 1 game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10751-belac93","name":"Belac93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10751_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T17:26:57-08:00","id":800833,"title":"","content":"The word you're looking for this kind of game is &quot;Crossover&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T17:28:16-08:00","id":800837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/800807-experiences-playing-a-multi-sourcbook-game?p=800833#post800833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The word you're looking for this kind of game is &quot;Crossover&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I'm pretty new to the terms. Thank you.<br /> Ah yes, I'm also a lurker, but a first time poster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10751,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10751-belac93","user":"Belac93","date":". 01-04-2016, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10751-belac93","name":"Belac93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10751_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T19:05:27-08:00","id":800873,"title":"","content":"I tried to ST a crossover game, it was a complete disaster; it was also the first game I tried to ST, and I haven't tried since.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T20:15:04-08:00","id":800914,"title":"","content":"I love using crossover elements in games, but only sparingly. Games where the players are all playing characters from different game lines almost never work out in my experience. It dilutes the themes of each game line and tends to require huge contrivances to get the player characters to work together. On the other hand, whenever I run (for example) a Vampire game, I like to have other supernaturals in the city, with their own problems and agendas, that can end up interacting with the player characters in various ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T00:20:45-08:00","id":801200,"title":"","content":"I ran a game that was primarily Changeling for more or less two years. We also had a Mage (and a second, briefly), a custom Changing Breed, and a Sin-Eater.<br /> <br /> I focused mostly on Blue Book threats, but I tried to spotlight each splat in whatever way we could. A trip to the Underworld. A trip to the Hedge. Tracking down rogue mages. That sort of thing.<br /> <br /> It went pretty great, but you do need to put restrictions. Putting a Vampire in a party with a Geist would have been unwise, for example. The biggest problem was making sure everyone had ways to refill their various energy stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T06:20:37-08:00","id":801325,"title":"","content":"I'm currently running a mortals --&gt; crossover game, and I think it's going quite well. In a crossover game, it's less important to stick to the general themes of the specific gamelines for each character (eg retaining your humanity for vampires, obsession over mysteries for mage, etc) and more important to find a central theme to tie all the characters together. Maybe all the characters are discovering who they truly are, or are all looking for something in common. <br /> <br /> Another thing that can help is keeping the game going between sessions. I often run solo scenes with my players via texts over the week, saving the group sessions for group scenes if I can. This can keep solo themes running for each character alongside the chronicle spanning themes.<br /> <br /> Finally, make sure you have a hand in character building, or have everyone discuss their ideas openly. While your party probably won't be balanced, you can at least try to ensure that no one is overshadowed, which can easily happen in a crossover game. If you have (for example) a werewolf built for social skills and a gangrel built for combat, there's going to be jealousy, because the wolf will still likely be better at combat. Every line has things that they are just better at, so try to get players to embrace that rather than trying to play across type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T06:30:01-08:00","id":801335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/800807-experiences-playing-a-multi-sourcbook-game?p=801325#post801325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, make sure you have a hand in character building, or have everyone discuss their ideas openly. While your party probably won't be balanced, you can at least try to ensure that no one is overshadowed, which can easily happen in a crossover game. If you have (for example) a werewolf built for social skills and a gangrel built for combat, there's going to be jealousy, because the wolf will still likely be better at combat. Every line has things that they are just better at, so try to get players to embrace that rather than trying to play across type.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. This is probably the most important advice. We played a huge crossover once where basically everyone was a different splat, and it worked due to a common enemy and embracing the strengths of our own splat rather than trying to go on other people's turf.<br /> <br /> The Werewolf was built for combat<br /> The Mage was intelligent beyond measure (But even still, just don't put a Mage in a crossover, they overshadow everyone without even trying)<br /> The Changeling was a social monster<br /> The Promethean was indestructible<br /> The mortal was a grounding point for all of us. A Touchstone for all others, if you will.<br /> <br /> The game lasted a few months before real life disbanded us. It was probably for the best; the scenario was becoming too weird for my suspension of disbelief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T06:40:39-08:00","id":801344,"title":"","content":"I don\u00b4t like to run full crossovers because each CofD game is deep and good enough for it\u00b4s own merits. If you mix PCs from different gamelines, you will not have a better game, you will get a more diluted one. In example, if you narrate a hunting scene, or a mage\u00b4s astral travel you will alienate other players. So you must put aside those scenes to keep the action going for everybody. It\u00b4s like having 3 small childs looking for your atention at the same time.<br /> If you use other supernaturals as NPCs, the things can work better because you have 100% control over them. In this case I just recommend to adapt the system to the game you\u00b4re runing. In example, If you\u00b4re running vampire game and a wild mage appears, don't use the full Mage the Awakening rules for Magic, just decide what the mage can do and throw some dice pools for it. It will save you A LOT of time.<br /> <br /> I know crossovers are popular, but for me are better in theory than in actual gameplay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3008-masa","name":"Masa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3008_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T10:40:56-08:00","id":808023,"title":"","content":"I've had a great experience playing a crossover in a VtR centric game. I was playing a Tremere Lich that was integrated into a vampire coterie. I was able to play off most of my abilities as the disciplines from an undisclosed bloodline. The other players never knew I was playing a mage until after the game ended. Good times were had by all.<br /> <br /> Of course this was in a 1ed game, so I'm not sure if the new 2ed mechanics would render this less doable.<br /> <br /> Our VtR Storyteller will be coming up soon in our group's GM rotation, and all of us are really looking forward to it. A new-ish player to this group has expressed an interest in playing a Promethian. Interesting times are on the horizon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T21:01:03-08:00","id":808434,"title":"","content":"Don't do it unless, you (the ST) are intimately familiar with all of the gamelines, and the players have shown they too are willing to become intimately familiar with their gameline. I was not, and my players were not and it was a terrible experience. Do I think it has to be this way? no, but I do not think it is for novices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T23:44:05-08:00","id":808489,"title":"","content":"Yes I agree with everyone that it's an extremely difficult thing to do and will in all likelihood fail. However, just remember that a failed gaming session isn't really all that bad a thing. Sometime's it's worth taking that risk to try something fun and innovate a bit with your storytelling. Just adding that in for perspective.<br /> <br /> That said, it's a very difficult challenge. Leaving aside the difficulties of the different themes and everything, just from a rules mastery perspective it can be challenging. It's hard enough to answer a question for a Mage player about the difference between a Vulgar and a Covert spell, but then if you're immediately asked a question by a Changeling player about how to access the Hedge through a Hollow it's even more difficult. It's hard to reference that many books so quickly so you'll probably have to memorize everything. Then you're also bound to get cross-over questions like whether Supernal magic is Vulgar inside the Hedge, and that's not easy to figure out or look up in the middle of a session.<br /> <br /> Right now is a really difficult time to do cross-over games as well. Half of the games are still only available in 1st Edition rules. Which means either you use 1st Edition rules for everything, tough if like me you've fallen in love with the 2nd Edition rules, or you try to update the rules yourself, or you run a hybrid game where not everyone is even following the same base system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/800807-experiences-playing-a-multi-sourcbook-game?p=800914#post800914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, whenever I run (for example) a Vampire game, I like to have other supernaturals in the city, with their own problems and agendas, that can end up interacting with the player characters in various ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do this too. Sometimes to probably ridiculous degrees. Right now I don't have any plans for Vampires to come into my current Mage Chronicle and yet I've got a detailed write-up of the city's vampiric political structure and a large number of vampire NPCs that I've designed. Still, I'm confident now that if a player decides to start looking into vampires I'll have that information close to hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T00:03:28-08:00","id":808496,"title":"","content":"Crossover games work exceedingly well when your players aren't actually interested in a gameline's theme and/or mood, but really enjoy the mechanics or the aesthetics or some combination of both. For example, if you have a player that wants to be a Daeva, be really good at social and have a lot of social merits, but isn't interested in Kindred politics or the struggle to retain humanity, he's going to fit right in a crossover, because what the player wants is to have her handsome vampire do social stuff. So long as you make sure the player gets what she wants out of her character, they'll be happy.<br /> <br /> Then, all you need to do is come up with an overarching plot that ties those characters together, whether because their territories/power bases/loved ones are in danger, or because they know each other from back when they were humans, or because some external force recruits them for a cause.<br /> <br /> For characters that are really into the gameline's theme and mood, you can simply give them regular times to explore them. It's in general a good ST practice to make sure each player gets their turn in the spotlight, so what better place to explore the gameline's theme and mood?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T00:49:56-08:00","id":808503,"title":"","content":"My first Chronicle that I'm running is a crossover, and it's doing fine. I got a mage, werewolf, &amp; sin eater in the troupe and while they tend to not care about each others splats antagonist. So I find giving them a problem that effect all of them is the best way to kerp them together. Also the God Machine is a very effective one to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T08:06:21-08:00","id":808709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/800807-experiences-playing-a-multi-sourcbook-game?p=808496#post808496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crossover games work exceedingly well when your players aren't actually interested in a gameline's theme and/or mood, but really enjoy the mechanics or the aesthetics or some combination of both. For example, if you have a player that wants to be a Daeva, be really good at social and have a lot of social merits, but isn't interested in Kindred politics or the struggle to retain humanity, he's going to fit right in a crossover, because what the player wants is to have her handsome vampire do social stuff. So long as you make sure the player gets what she wants out of her character, they'll be happy.<br /> <br /> Then, all you need to do is come up with an overarching plot that ties those characters together, whether because their territories/power bases/loved ones are in danger, or because they know each other from back when they were humans, or because some external force recruits them for a cause.<br /> <br /> For characters that are really into the gameline's theme and mood, you can simply give them regular times to explore them. It's in general a good ST practice to make sure each player gets their turn in the spotlight, so what better place to explore the gameline's theme and mood?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Exactly ! I had a crossover game that included vampires, changeling, werewolf and demon. We are all experienced players and it lasted about a year before RL jobs split the game apart. The Vampire actually fell in love with the changeling and that was very interesting to explore that. The Vampire and the werewolf became BFF's and the demon (who was added later) decided to make her character Fall because she saw that the changeling was doing what he wanted to do to be happy, that he didnt have to follow some set of rules set forth by the people around him. we took on Mages tried to mess with time. We Fought things from the gauntlet, the Camarilla imploded and the vampire actually became the new Prince of the city... which then started a war with the Daeva and the Nos... then there was months of trying to get all the &quot;splats&quot; to coexist which was another fun arch to explore. keep in mind this is a short paragraph trying to explain a year of weekly gaming. it might not make sense, but it was a blast and successful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T09:43:16-08:00","id":808774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/800807-experiences-playing-a-multi-sourcbook-game?p=808709#post808709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Exactly ! I had a crossover game that included vampires, changeling, werewolf and demon. We are all experienced players and it lasted about a year before RL jobs split the game apart. The Vampire actually fell in love with the changeling and that was very interesting to explore that. The Vampire and the werewolf became BFF's and the demon (who was added later) decided to make her character Fall because she saw that the changeling was doing what he wanted to do to be happy, that he didnt have to follow some set of rules set forth by the people around him. we took on Mages tried to mess with time. We Fought things from the gauntlet, the Camarilla imploded and the vampire actually became the new Prince of the city... which then started a war with the Daeva and the Nos... then there was months of trying to get all the &amp;quot;splats&amp;quot; to coexist which was another fun arch to explore. keep in mind this is a short paragraph trying to explain a year of weekly gaming. it might not make sense, but it was a blast and successful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a great story. Could you give a run down of the characters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T12:10:26-08:00","id":808923,"title":"","content":"My character was one of the vampires. He was a Daeva. young fellow freshly turned who loved to party. He was a stripper at a Daeva owned club.<br /> The changeling was of the Summer Court.. the emotions and desires one? I honestly am not too familiar. He worked a little herbal remedy store that catered to changelings mostly, but some humans. That's pretty much how the changeling and the daeva hooked up because neither had a good track record on controlling their desires.<br /> The werewolf was sort of in denial about what he was. He owned a gun store in town, and was an avid game hunter<br /> The Demon was a guardian?... we loved to poke fun at him and call him a transformer... He fell for the changeling and vowed to protect him.<br /> There was another vampire girl who was also a Daeva but she fled hunters in Montreal to settle in Minneapolis where the story took place.<br /> Oh she had a ghoul who I played so she wouldnt have to have conversations with herself and the ST wouldnt have to take on one more ST. He was a bit of a psychopath and he was her Sire's ghoul, but the Sire was killed by the hunters and he decided to stay on with her.... ( because really there was no other choice for a ghoul.. )<br /> <br /> <br /> Is that what you were looking for? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":".  Added the ghoul 01-14-2016, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T07:06:28-08:00","id":809561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belac93</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/800807-experiences-playing-a-multi-sourcbook-game#post800807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are your experiences playing a game with multiple types of creature? Like having a vampire, mage, and 2 changelings in 1 game?</div> </div> </div> </div>I love Mage. But It is overpowered with regards to Vam even new Vamp using dynamic blood magic. The Same with WereWolf.<br /> Adapt Witchhunters and Second Sight to Second Edition and use that to build mages.<br /> I've been Toying with adapting Dynamic Blood Sorcery with changes for Human with the Cruac being a bloody Black Art that taints the practitioners with the taint of the curse. It does fit the lore of killing evil witches and some of them rising as vamps.<br /> <br /> I have not figured what to do about weres in a vamp game other than using the doomed infrome the Werewolf chroniclers guide. Or the ones based on vice from the same book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","user":"Chattnos","date":".  clarity 01-15-2016, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}